cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use TrialDiff or its Evidence Record datasets, please cite this
  repository. Individual Evidence Records can additionally be cited by their
  event_id and citation_text.
title: "TrialDiff: deterministic Evidence Records for ClinicalTrials.gov amendment history"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Brandes
    given-names: Amadeus
    affiliation: Independent researcher
repository-code: "https://github.com/AMBRA7592/trialdiff"
url: "https://trialdiff.vercel.app"
license: Apache-2.0
# Data (records/, event_class_records_*, CALIBRATION_*, corpora/) and project
# prose documentation are CC-BY-4.0; see DATA_LICENSE.md.
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.20801956
    description: >-
      Concept DOI for the TrialDiff event-class Evidence Record dataset
      (all versions; v0.1.2 is 10.5281/zenodo.21755258 and v0.1.1 is
      10.5281/zenodo.20816639). See ERRATA.md E1 for the corrected v0.1.2
      release.
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21755258
    description: Version DOI for the corrected v0.1.2 event-class dataset.
abstract: >-
  TrialDiff converts public ClinicalTrials.gov record-version history into
  deterministic, hash-verifiable, claim-bounded Evidence Records: exact
  changed paths, source hashes, deterministic classification rules, timing
  context, and explicit claims-supported / claims-not-supported boundaries.
  Severity/triage labels are deterministic, reproducible, uncalibrated
  metadata; the v0.2/v0.2.1 blinded calibration attempt failed its
  pre-registered gate and is published in full.
keywords:
  - clinical-trials
  - clinicaltrials-gov
  - meta-research
  - protocol-amendments
  - provenance
  - reproducibility
